---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/legal-layout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  canonicalPath="/cookies"
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="How Docita uses cookies, local storage, and related technologies"
  lastUpdated="March 15, 2026"
>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">1. What Are Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website.
      They allow the website to remember your actions and preferences over time, so
      you do not have to re-enter them whenever you return or move between pages.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">2. How We Use Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">Docita uses cookies and similar technologies to:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Keep you signed in to your account across sessions</li>
      <li>Remember your preferences (language, theme, currency)</li>
      <li>Understand how the application is used to improve it</li>
      <li>Detect and prevent fraud and security threats</li>
      <li>Ensure pages load correctly and features function as expected</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">3. Types of Cookies We Use</h2>

    <h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">3.1 Strictly Necessary Cookies</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      These cookies are essential for the website to function and cannot be switched
      off. They are usually set in response to actions you take, such as logging in
      or filling in forms.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-hidden rounded-[var(--radius)] border">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b bg-muted/50">
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium text-foreground">Cookie</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium text-foreground">Purpose</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium text-foreground">Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b">
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-foreground">auth_token</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Maintains your authenticated session</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Session</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b">
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-foreground">csrf_token</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Protects against cross-site request forgery</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Session</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-foreground">tenant_id</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Identifies your facility workspace</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Session</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">3.2 Functional Cookies</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      These cookies allow the website to remember choices you have made to provide
      enhanced, personalized features. Disabling them may affect your experience.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-hidden rounded-[var(--radius)] border">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b bg-muted/50">
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium text-foreground">Cookie</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium text-foreground">Purpose</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium text-foreground">Duration</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b">
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-foreground">theme</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Remembers your light/dark mode preference</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">1 year</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b">
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-foreground">currency_pref</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Remembers your selected display currency</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">24 hours</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-foreground">locale</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">Remembers your language preference</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2">1 year</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-medium text-foreground">3.3 Analytics Cookies</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      These cookies help us understand how visitors interact with our website by
      collecting and reporting information anonymously. All analytics data is
      aggregated and does not identify individual users.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We do not use third-party advertising or behavioral tracking cookies. Any
      analytics we collect is processed in-house or via privacy-first tools that do
      not share data with advertisers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">4. Local Storage</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      In addition to cookies, we use browser local storage to save certain
      preferences (such as detected currency and user-interface state). Local
      storage data does not leave your device by itself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">5. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Some features of Docita rely on third-party services that may set their own
      cookies:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong>Razorpay</strong> - payment processing; cookies are set during
        checkout and are governed by
        <a
          class="mx-1 text-primary hover:underline"
          href="https://razorpay.com/privacy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Razorpay privacy policy
        </a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AWS CloudFront</strong> - content delivery; may set cookies for
        load balancing and security.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We do not use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, or other advertising-platform
      trackers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">6. Managing Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">You can control and manage cookies in several ways:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong>Browser settings:</strong> Most browsers allow you to refuse or
        delete cookies through settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>In-app preferences:</strong> Functional preferences (theme,
        language, currency) can be changed directly inside the Docita app.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Clearing local storage:</strong> You can clear local storage any
        time via browser site-data controls.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Disabling strictly necessary cookies will prevent login and key product
      functionality.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">7. Compliance</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Our cookie practices are consistent with the Digital Personal Data
      Protection Act, 2023 (India) and the Information Technology Act, 2000.
      We do not use cookies to build advertising profiles or share data for
      marketing purposes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in
      technology or regulation. The "Last updated" date on this page will be
      revised accordingly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-foreground">9. Contact us</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">If you have questions about our cookie practices:</p>
    <div class="mt-4 rounded-[var(--radius)] border bg-card p-4">
      <p class="font-medium text-foreground">Docita Data Protection Team</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Email:
        <a class="ml-1 text-primary hover:underline" href="mailto:admin@docita.work">admin@docita.work</a>
      </p>
      <p>Address: Aparna Cyberscape, Nalagandla, Hyderabad, India</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
